        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. US plans to slash fighter jets, warships to NATO in Europe, NY Times reports Issued on: 12/06/2026 - 16:04 The United States plans to slash the number of fighter jets and warships it provides to NATO in Europe, the New York Times reported on Thursday. The reported cutbacks come as European nations race to bolster their defense capacities since Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022 sparked fears that Moscow could attack a NATO country. France 24's Rochelle Ferguson-Bouyahi takes a closer look. As alcohol returns to World Cup, Ecuador president tells fans to drink up 12/06/2026 'All of us of are migrants,' pope says in Canary Islands as Spain trip wraps up 12/06/2026 First group of Nigerians returns home after anti-immigration protests in South Africa 12/06/2026 Wrapped in paradox: Most inclusive tournament in terms of countries participating yet many excluded 12/06/2026 Congo's 1974 World Cup pioneers 12/06/2026 David Hockney, iconic British artist, dies at 88 12/06/2026 'Deep mistrust' in Tehran as Iran plays down Trump's deal claims 12/06/2026 'Extremely complex legislation: Can they agree on common rules to manage migration together?\" 12/06/2026 Europe Unfilled hotels and empty seats raise doubts over expected World Cup windfall 12/06/2026"
